{
  "title": "SI Dislocation & Crescent Fractures",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/trauma/1031/si-dislocation-and-crescent-fractures",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Aug 28 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Sacroiliac (SI) dislocations and crescent fractures include a spectrum of injuries involving the pelvis which can lead to instability and pelvic malalignment.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis requires pelvic radiographs with CT scan.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is generally operative with reduction and fixation of both the anterior and posterior pelvis ring as needed.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Spectrum of injuries that include",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**incomplete (Sacroiliac) SI dislocation**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "posterior SI ligaments remain intact",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "rotationally unstable",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**complete SI dislocations**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "posterior SI ligaments ruptured",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "vertically and rotationally unstable",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**SI fracture-dislocation (crescent fracture)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "iliac wing fracture that enters the SI joint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "injury to posterior ligaments vary",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "combination of vertical iliac fx and SI dislocation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "posterior ilium remains attached to sacrum by posterior SI ligaments",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "anterior ilium dislocates from sacrum with internal rotation deformity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "when ilium fragment remains with sacrum it is termed a crescent fracture",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Pathophysiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Mechanism of injury",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "lateral compression force",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "usually high energy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Pathoanatomy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "degree of injury to posterior structures determines pelvic stability",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Iliac wing fractures may be associated with open wounds and may involve bowel entrapment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Ligaments",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "the SI joint is stabilized by the posterior pelvic ligaments",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "sacrospinous",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "sacrotuberous",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "anterior sacroiliac",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "posterior sacroiliac",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Nerves",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "the L5 nerve root crosses the sacral ala approximately 2 cm medial to SI joint",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Blood supply",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "the superior gluteal artery runs across SI joint",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "exits pelvis via greater sciatic notch",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "No classification system specifically for SI injury",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "included in Young- Burgess and Tile classification of pelvic fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "crescent fractures described as LC-2 injury according to Young-Burgess",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1031/images/untitled-7-595x449.jpg",
                  "caption": "Young Burgess Classification of Pelvic Ring injuries"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pelvic pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical Exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "assess hemodynamic status",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "perform detailed neurological exam",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "abdominal assessment to look for distention",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "rectal exam",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "examine urethral meatus for blood",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1031/images/Xray%20-%20AP%20-%20crescent%20fx%20(wheeless)_moved.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP pelvis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "inlet and outlet views",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT scan",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1031/images/CT-%20axial%20-%20crescent%20fx%20(wheeless)_moved.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "evaluation of sacral fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "posterior pelvis better delineated",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "immediate skeletal traction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "vertical translation of the hemipelvis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "anterior ring ORIF",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "incomplete SI dislocations with pubic symphyseal diastasis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "anterior and posterior ring ORIF",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "complete SI dislocations",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "vertically unstable require anterior and posterior pelvic ring fixation",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "ORIF of ilium",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "crescent fracture",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "required to restore posterior SI ligaments and pelvic stability",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Closed Reduction and Percutaneous Fixation**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "positioning",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "intraoperative traction may aid in reduction",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "small midline bump under sacrum may assist with SI screw placement",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "imaging",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "inlet view",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "shows anterior-posterior position of SI joint(s) for screw placement",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1031/images/inlet.jpg",
                          "caption": "inlet view pelvis"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outlet view",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "shows cephalad-caudad position of SI joint(s) for screw placement",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1031/images/outlet.jpg",
                          "caption": "outlet view, pelvis"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "lateral sacral view",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "ensures safe placement of SI or sacral screws relative to the anterior cortex of the sacral ala and the nerve root tunnel",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "complications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**L5 nerve root at risk** with anterior perforation of iliosacral screw as nerve goes inferiorly over sacral ala",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**ORIF**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "anterior approach",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "lateral window with elevation iliacus back to SI joint",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "posterior approach",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "for fixation of crescent fragment to intact ilium",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "fixation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "plates",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**iliosacral lag screws (SI screws)**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**DVT**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "35%-50%",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Neurological injury**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Loss of reduction and failure of fixation**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Primarily based on accurate and stable reduction of SI joint",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
